      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: Boots (album). Boots is a 1966 debut studio album by Nancy Sinatra. The album was produced by Lee Hazlewood. Billy Strange was the arranger and conductor. The album is titled after the song on the album \"These Boots Are Made for Walkin'\", which became a #1 hit for Sinatra. Most of the other songs on the album are covers of then-recent hits.",
